# Line ending policy.
#
# Every file in this repository uses LF, in the repository and in the working tree, on
# every platform. `rustfmt.toml` already sets `newline_style = "Unix"`; this makes git
# agree with it.
#
# This is not cosmetic. `crates/aprsr-web/static/` holds generated assets that are also
# committed, and CI checks they are current with a plain `git diff --exit-code`. Git's
# Windows default (`core.autocrlf=true`) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which would make
# that diff non-empty on every Windows run whether or not anything had actually gone stale.
# Pinning `eol=lf` means a checkout on Windows, macOS and Linux produces identical bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The dashboard bundles are produced byte-for-byte by esbuild and Tailwind and compared the
# same way. Keep git out of their contents entirely rather than trusting the heuristic.
crates/aprsr-web/static/** -text

# Snapshot files are compared literally by insta; a rewritten line ending is a false diff.
*.snap -text
